course: dictionary
lesson: 4215
title: Abbreviations: short words for long names
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer name or phrase. GPS is an abbreviation: its letters stand for Global Positioning System. You do not need to know the full name to understand the word, but knowing it helps you work out what the word means.
explain: Read the words around GPS for clues. «Turn on the GPS» tells you it is something you switch on, like a device. «Each GPS satellite keeps perfect time» tells you it has something to do with satellites in space. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: GPS can mean the system itself or a device or app that uses it. In «a GPS tracker» it is a small device, and in «GPS coordinates» it means numbers that show exactly where something is. Look at the words next to GPS, because they often give the clue.
fact: GPS is an abbreviation, a short form of Global Positioning System.
fact: «GPS» means a system that uses satellites to show exactly where you are on Earth.
fact: «GPS» can also mean a device or app that gives directions, as in «turn on the GPS».
fact: «GPS» appears in phrases such as «GPS tracker» and «GPS coordinates».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Turn on the GPS.» What does GPS mean here? | A brand of microchip | A kind of rain | A type of bus stop sign | *A device or app that gives directions
exercise: «Each GPS satellite keeps perfect time with an atomic clock.» What is GPS short for? | General Post Office | Great Public Service | Green Power Station | *Global Positioning System
exercise: «Live bus stop signs use the GPS position each bus sends.» What does each bus send? | Its driver's name | *Its GPS position | Its ticket prices | Its luggage
test: «A GPS tracker» on a pet helps people see where it is. What does GPS mean in this phrase? | A kind of pet food | A fast type of train | *A small device that shows where something is | A map printed on paper
test: Which is the best way to check the meaning of an abbreviation like GPS in a sentence? | Ignore the sentence and guess | Skip the word and never come back to it | Change the word to a longer one with no meaning | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
exam: «Rescuers used GPS to find the lost walkers.» What does GPS help the rescuers do? | *Find exactly where the walkers are | Sing a song to cheer them up | Cook a meal for the walkers | Pitch a tent for the night
